                "senderName": "NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 23 at 12:29PM MDT until October 25 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of south central New Mexico, including the\nfollowing areas, East Central Tularosa Basin/Alamogordo, Otero\nMesa, Southeast Tularosa Basin and West Central Tularosa\nBasin/White Sands and southwest Texas, including the following\nareas, Eastern/Central El Paso County, Northern Hudspeth\nHighlands/Hueco Mountains, Rio Grande Valley of Eastern El\nPaso/Western Hudspeth Counties, Rio Grande Valley of Eastern\nHudspeth County, Salt Basin, Southern Hudspeth Highlands and\nWestern El Paso County.\n\n* WHEN...From Saturday evening through late Saturday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas. Low-water\ncrossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Several rounds of thunderstorms are expected to move through the\nregion between this evening and late Saturday night. Widespread\nrainfall amounts of up to 1\" are likely with localized areas\nreceiving 2-3\" resulting in flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
