                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 23 at 12:15PM MDT until October 24 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of north central and west central New Mexico,\nincluding the following areas, in north central New Mexico, Far\nNorthwest Highlands, Jemez Mountains and Northwest Highlands. In\nwest central New Mexico, West Central Highlands and West Central\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...Through this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Flooding may occur\nin poor drainage and urban areas. Low-water crossings may be\nflooded. Storm drains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms will redevelop\nthis afternoon. While rainfall rates will not be as high as\nyesterday, it will not take much additional rainfall to worsen\nrunoff that will lead to flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/abq/EmergencyPrepFlood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
