                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 23 at 12:15PM MDT until October 25 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of central New Mexico, including the following\narea, South Central Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 PM MDT this evening through late Saturday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A longer duration period of numerous showers and thunderstorms\nwill set up this evening, with activity redeveloping again in the\nafternoon Saturday and persisting into Saturday evening. Recent\nwildfire burn scars in Lincoln county remain vulnerable to abrupt\nrunoff and flash flooding. While individual showers and\nthunderstorms will typically produce rainfall amounts of 0.25 to\n0.75 inch, multiple rounds of storms will increase the risk of\nflash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/abq/EmergencyPrepFlood",
