                "senderName": "NWS Pueblo CO",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 23 at 7:40AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible new\nFlood Warnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be\nprepared to take action should flooding develop.",
