                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 22 at 11:28AM MDT until October 24 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "...The National Weather Service in Albuquerque has issued a Flood\nWatch for the following rivers in New Mexico...\n\nAnimas River At Farmington affecting Northwest Plateau zone.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Animas River at Farmington.\n\n* WHEN...From Friday evening to Saturday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 10.0 feet, Portions of the riverwalk in Farmington are\nflooded. Local overbank flooding is occurring along the lower\nAnimas River.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:30 AM MDT Thursday the stage was 6.4 feet.\n- Forecast...Flood stage may be reached late tomorrow evening.\n- Flood stage is 10.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "If you are in the watch area, remain alert to possible flooding.\n\nResidents and those with interests near the river should monitor\nrising water levels and be prepared for possible Flood Warnings.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/abq.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Friday afternoon at noon MDT.",
